WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.740
Finally, let us briefly consider how we
should prepare.

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:14.600
I encourage you to study Matthew 24 and
25, together with the Life-study messages
on

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.300
these chapters.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:21.854
The Lord's return has two aspects: first,
He comes secretly to take the overcoming

00:00:21.854 --> 00:00:23.880
believers who are mature in life.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.620
Then the Lord will come openly.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.420
Second, we must watch and be ready.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:34.467
The days of Noah are before us. As living
believers, we should still carry on our

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:35.280
normal work.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:39.440
As we live in the mingled spirit, we will
be raptured.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:44.737
The Lord says He will come like a thief
for treasure. We should be worth His
coming

00:00:44.737 --> 00:00:45.320
to take us.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:50.767
The more of Christ we have within, and the
more mature we are, the more we are worth

00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:51.480
His taking.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:58.483
Third, be faithful and prudent stewards,
providing food at the proper time in the

00:00:58.483 --> 00:00:59.280
church life.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:04.020
We should not only enjoy what others
supply; we must also supply others.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.320
The evil servant thinks, My master is
delayed.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.280
Do not think that way. The day of the
Lord's coming may arrive suddenly.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:22.508
Be prudent virgins who hear and practice
the Lord's word, using the time to mature

00:01:22.508 --> 00:01:23.260
in life.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:30.714
The foolish virgins did not prepare oil,
because they heard the Lord's word but did

00:01:30.714 --> 00:01:32.000
not practice it.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:40.016
We must be prudent. Especially after
hearing this message, we should prepare
oil

00:01:40.016 --> 00:01:40.880
every day.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:49.796
Be faithful and good servants, using the
gifts the Lord has given us to preach the

00:01:49.796 --> 00:01:52.280
gospel, shepherd, and serve.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:56.840
Do not bury your gift like the servant
with one talent.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:03.120
Merely maintaining what we have is not
enough. We must gain more and mature in
life.

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:07.740
Second Peter says we have the prophetic
word made more firm.

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:14.227
We should heed it as a lamp shining in a
dark place, until the day dawns and the

00:02:14.227 --> 00:02:16.680
morning star rises in our hearts.
